      'through' => 'PostsTags',\n        'conditions' => ['PostsTags.primary' => 0]\n    ]\n);\n```\n\nController/add:\n\n```\n$post = $this->Posts->newEntity([\n    'tags' => ['_ids' => [1,2]]\n]);\n```\n\nThis errors out since `Marshaller::_loadBelongsToMany` tries to do this, and PostsTags isn't on that query:\n`SELECT `Tags`.`id` AS `Tags__id`, `Tags`.`name` AS `Tags__name` FROM `tags` `Tags` WHERE (`PostsTags`.`primary` = '0' AND `Tags`.`id` in (1,2))`\n\nI've tried changing the association strategy but that didn't help. Is there something in the through Table I should be using for this?\n\nThanks\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cakephp/cakephp/issues/comments/61693176/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"patrickconroy","id":954577,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk1NDU3Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/954577?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrickconroy","html_url":"https://github.com/patrickconroy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrickconroy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrickconroy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrickconroy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrickconroy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrickconroy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrickconroy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrickconroy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrickconroy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrickconroy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cakephp/cakephp/issues/comments/61745808","html_url":"https://github